    "name": "intraday_volatility_activity_lead_lag_asymmetry_236p",
    "direction": "higher",
    "formula": "Within each 120-close half, form 119 adjacent log returns r_j and destination-bar activity a_j=log1p(amount_{j+1}). Across the 118 adjacent return/activity pairs per half, pooled to 236, return Corr(abs(r_j),a_{j+1}) - Corr(a_j,abs(r_{j+1})) using equal-position population Pearson correlations.",
    "economic_hypothesis": "Higher reactive-minus-anticipatory association indicates activity arrives to absorb completed price shocks rather than foreshadowing the next shock, potentially supporting stronger next-open-to-third-close performance.",
